# Cursor Rules & Agent Boundaries

- Do not make changes or commit directly to `main`. Always work on `develop` or a feature branch.
- Commit granularly as logical tasks are completed.
- Commit messages must be strictly a single line, brief and direct (e.g. `feat: ...`, `fix: ...`, `chore: ...`).
- Never add co-author trailers (`Co-authored-by:`) or any agent attribution under any circumstances.
- Organize code using directories: Group related functions and components into feature folders so the project is easy to navigate without opening files.
- Respect git hooks configured in `.githooks/`.
